{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' screening_policy.md\npython - <<'PY'\nimport csv,json,itertools,collections\nfor p in ['customers.csv','dev/customers_dev.csv','dev/labels_dev.csv']:\n print('\\\\nFILE',p)\n with open(p,encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n  rd=csv.DictReader(f); print('fields',rd.fieldnames)\n  for x in itertools.islice(rd,5): print(x)\nwith open('watchlist.json',encoding='utf-8') as f: d=json.load(f)\nprint('\\\\nwatch type',type(d),'len',len(d) if hasattr(d,'__len__') else '')\nif isinstance(d,dict): print('keys',d.keys()); vals=next((v for v in d.values() if isinstance(v,list)),None); print('listlen',len(vals) if vals else None); d=vals or []\nfor x in d[:4]: print(x)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' screening_policy.md\npython - <<'PY'\nimport csv,json,itertools,collections\nfor p in ['customers.csv','dev/customers_dev.csv','dev/labels_dev.csv']:\n print('\\\\nFILE',p)\n with open(p,encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n  rd=csv.DictReader(f); print('fields',rd.fieldnames)\n  for x in itertools.islice(rd,5): print(x)\nwith open('watchlist.json',encoding='utf-8') as f: d=json.load(f)\nprint('\\\\nwatch type',type(d),'len',len(d) if hasattr(d,'__len__') else '')\nif isinstance(d,dict): print('keys',d.keys()); vals=next((v for v in d.values() if isinstance(v,list)),None); print('listlen',len(vals) if vals else None); d=vals or []\nfor x in d[:4]: print(x)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Sanctions Screening Policy\n\nThis policy defines when a customer record matches a watchlist entry. The\nverifier grades outcomes only: for every customer in `/app/customers.csv`,\n`decision` must be `MATCH` with the correct `matched_uid`, or `NO_MATCH`.\n\n## Inputs\n\n`/app/watchlist.json` is a list of entries with `uid`, `type`\n(`individual`, `entity`, `vessel`), `primary_name`, `script_name` (the name in\nits original script when the person is from an Arabic-, Persian- or\nCyrillic-script culture, else null), `aliases` (each with `name` and\n`strength` `strong` or `weak`), `dob` (`YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY`, or empty),\n`nationalities`, `ids` (each with `type` and `number`) and `programs`. For some\nindividuals `primary_name` is the original-script name itself; those entries\nmay have no Latin spelling anywhere.\n\n`/app/customers.csv` has `customer_id, full_name, dob, nationality, id_type,\nid_number, type`. `dob` may be a full date, a year, a year-month, or empty.\n\n## Rule 1: identifiers\n\nIf the customer's `id_type` and `id_number` equal an entry's identifier\n(`passport`, `registration`, or `imo`), the customer matches that entry\nregardless of the name or date of birth. An identifier that matches no entry\nneither confirms nor rules out anything; the customer is then judged on name\nand date of birth like any other.\n\n## Rule 2: name equivalence\n\nTwo names refer to the same person when, after normalization, the given name\nand the family name correspond. Names correspond across all of the following\nvariations. The development sample illustrates them; it does not exhaust them.\nThe batch uses romanization conventions (for example French, German, Polish\nand Gulf spellings of Arabic and Russian names, Cantonese surnames, sun-letter\nassimilation of the Arabic article) that do not appear in the development\nsample, and it stacks several conventions on one name.\n\n- Transliteration into Latin script from Arabic, Persian and Cyrillic under any\n  common romanization (for example Muhammad/Mohammed/Mohamed/Mohamad,\n  Abdul Rahman/Abdurrahman/Abd al-Rahman, Hussein/Husain/Hussain/Husayn,\n  Sergei/Sergey/Serguei/Sergej, Fedorov/Fyodorov/Fedoroff, Yevgeny/Evgeny/Eugene),\n  including matching a Latin customer name against an entry that only has an\n  original-script name.\n- Chinese names under pinyin and Wade-Giles/Cantonese romanizations\n  (Zhang/Chang, Wang/Wong, Li/Lee, Zhou/Chou/Chow, Xiao Ming/Xiaoming/Hsiao-Ming),\n  in either family-name-first or given-name-first order.\n- Western nicknames and diacritic variants (William/Bill, Katherine/Kate,\n  Jose/José, Mueller/Müller/Muller, Nguyen/Nguyễn), middle initials, and\n  hyphenated versus spaced compound surnames.\n- Name order (family name first, with or without a comma), presence or absence\n  of Russian patronymics, presence or absence of Arabic nasab elements\n  (`bin`/`ibn`/`ben` + father's name), and presence or absence of the Arabic\n  article (`al-`, `el-`, `Al `, attached `Al`).\n- Feminine Russian surname forms (Ivanova/Ivanov).\n\nNames do not correspond when the given name or the family name is a different\nname (Hassan is not Hussein, Ahmadi is not Ahmadi-with-a-different-given-name,\nAl-Noor Trading is not Al-Noor Shipping). A single shared given name or a\nsingle shared family name is not a name match.\n\n## Rule 3: aliases\n\nA `strong` alias is an alternative name of the entry and participates in\nRule 2 exactly like `primary_name`. A `weak` alias (a nickname or nom de\nguerre) matches a customer only when the customer's name equals the alias and\nRule 4 corroborates with an identical full date of birth, or Rule 1 applies.\nA weak alias alone never produces a match.\n\n## Rule 4: date of birth\n\nDates of birth are compared only when both sides have one. A full customer\ndate must equal the entry's full date. A customer year or year-month must be\na prefix of the entry's date. Any disagreement rules the candidate out (the\ncustomer is a different person with a similar name). A missing date on either\nside neither confirms nor rules out.\n\n## Rule 5: entities and vessels\n\nEntity names correspond when all name words correspond after removing legal\nform designators (LLC, L.L.C., Limited Liability Company, Ltd, Limited, S.A.,\nGmbH, JSC, Joint Stock Company, AO, OAO, PJSC, Co., Company, FZE, FZ-LLC and\nsimilar), leading `The`, punctuation, and the words `and`/`&`; case is\nignored. Vessel names correspond after removing prefixes such as `M/V`, `MV`,\n`M/T`, `MT`, `Vessel`. Identifiers (`registration`, `imo`) match under Rule 1.\n\n## Rule 6: nationality\n\nNationality is informational and does not confirm or rule out a match.\n\n## Output\n\n`/app/decisions.csv` with a header row `customer_id,decision,matched_uid`,\nexactly one row per customer in the batch, `decision` in `{MATCH, NO_MATCH}`,\nand `matched_uid` set to the entry `uid` for every `MATCH`. When more than one\nentry could match, choose the one supported by an identifier, then by a date\nof birth, then the lowest `uid` (string order). Closeness of spelling is not a\ntie-breaker: two entries with the same name and different dates of birth are\ntwo people, and a customer without a date of birth resolves to the lower `uid`.\n\n## Scoring\n\nThe batch is scored against hidden labels produced by the same process as\n`/app/dev/labels_dev.csv`. The task passes only if all of the following hold on\nthe batch: overall recall of true matches at least 0.97 and overall precision\nat least 0.97; recall at least 0.90 within every true-match variation class;\nfalse-positive rate at most 0.05 within every look-alike decoy class and at\nmost 0.01 among unrelated customers; and at least 0.97 of correct matches\ncarry the correct `matched_uid`. The development sample reports the same\nclasses so you can measure yourself before the batch is scored.\n\nFILE customers.csv\nfields ['customer_id', 'full_name', 'dob', 'nationality', 'id_type', 'id_number', 'type']\n{'customer_id': 'C766735', 'full_name': 'Sapphire Textiles, Limited Liability Company', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'SA', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'entity'}\n{'customer_id': 'C885994', 'full_name': 'Susan Pedersen', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'FR', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'individual'}\n{'customer_id': 'C741089', 'full_name': 'Hui-Hai Zeng', 'dob': '1980-03-20', 'nationality': 'SG', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'individual'}\n{'customer_id': 'C930138', 'full_name': 'PHOENIX INDUSTRIES L.L.C.', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'HK', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'entity'}\n{'customer_id': 'C337970', 'full_name': 'Paco Andersen', 'dob': '1971-11-12', 'nationality': 'MX', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'individual'}\n\nFILE dev/customers_dev.csv\nfields ['customer_id', 'full_name', 'dob', 'nationality', 'id_type', 'id_number', 'type']\n{'customer_id': 'D165351', 'full_name': 'Fatimmih Moussavi', 'dob': '1959-01-23', 'nationality': 'IR', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'individual'}\n{'customer_id': 'D427534', 'full_name': 'Tabriz & Partners', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'SY', 'id_type': 'registration', 'id_number': 'REG-274137', 'type': 'entity'}\n{'customer_id': 'D321795', 'full_name': 'Niloufar Ebrahemmi', 'dob': '1955-06', 'nationality': 'AF', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'individual'}\n{'customer_id': 'D755535', 'full_name': 'MT Coral Queen Queen', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'RU', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'vessel'}\n{'customer_id': 'D283347', 'full_name': 'Falcon Electronics FZE', 'dob': '', 'nationality': 'SY', 'id_type': '', 'id_number': '', 'type': 'entity'}\n\nFILE dev/labels_dev.csv\nfields ['customer_id', 'expected_decision', 'expected_uid', 'class']\n{'customer_id': 'D165351', 'expected_decision': 'NO_MATCH', 'expected_uid': '', 'class': 'D2_near_name'}\n{'customer_id': 'D427534', 'expected_decision': 'NO_MATCH', 'expected_uid': '', 'class': 'D7_id_unlisted'}\n{'customer_id': 'D321795', 'expected_decision': 'NO_MATCH', 'expected_uid': '', 'class': 'D5_partial_dob_conflict'}\n{'customer_id': 'D755535', 'expected_decision': 'NO_MATCH', 'expected_uid': '', 'class': 'R2_random_vessel'}\n{'customer_id': 'D283347', 'expected_decision': 'NO_MATCH', 'expected_uid': '', 'class': 'D4_entity_near_name'}\n\nwatch type <class 'list'> len 2100\n{'uid': 'SDN-98923', 'type': 'individual', 'primary_name': 'Omid Nazari', 'script_name': 'امید نظری', 'aliases': [{'name': 'Omed Nazari', 'strength': 'strong'}], 'dob': '1961-01-14', 'nationalities': ['AF'], 'ids': [], 'programs': ['SDGT']}\n{'uid': 'SDN-36851', 'type': 'individual', 'primary_name': 'Francisco Schmidt', 'script_name': None, 'aliases': [{'name': 'Francisco A. Schmidt', 'strength': 'strong'}], 'dob': '1960-01-26', 'nationalities': ['MX'], 'ids': [], 'programs': ['DPRK']}\n{'uid': 'SDN-97083', 'type': 'entity', 'primary_name': 'Tabriz Metals Corp', 'script_name': None, 'aliases': [], 'dob': '', 'nationalities': ['CA'], 'ids': [{'type': 'registration', 'number': 'REG-668565'}], 'programs': ['NPWMD']}\n{'uid': 'SDN-86414', 'type': 'individual', 'primary_name': 'يوسف حمدان', 'script_name': 'يوسف حمدان', 'aliases': [], 'dob': '', 'nationalities': ['SY'], 'ids': [], 'programs': ['SYRIA']}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport csv,json,collections,re\nwith open('watchlist.json',encoding='utf8') as f:w=json.load(f)\nprint('watch types',collections.Counter(x['type'] for x in w))\nprint('script',collections.Counter('none' if not x.get('script_name') else ('same' if x['script_name']==x['primary_name'] else 'other') for x in w))\nprint('alias strengths',collections.Counter(a['strength'] for x in w for a in x['aliases']))\nprint('dob shapes',collections.Counter(len(x.get('dob','')) for x in w))\nprint('ids',collections.Counter(i['type'] for x in w for i in x['ids']))\nwith open('dev/labels_dev.csv') as f:l=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('\\\\nlabels',collections.Counter(x['expected_decision'] for x in l))\nprint('classes')\nfor k,v in sorted(collections.Counter(x['class'] for x in l).items()):print(k,v)\nwith open('dev/customers_dev.csv') as f:c={x['customer_id']:x for x in csv.DictReader(f)}\nby={x['uid']:x for x in w}\nprint('\\\\nmatch class examples:')\nfor cls in sorted({x['class'] for x in l}):\n xs=[x for x in l if x['class']==cls][:5]\n print('\\\\n',cls)\n for y in xs:\n  z=c[y['customer_id']]; e=by.get(y['expected_uid'])\n  print(z,'=>', y['expected_uid'], (e['primary_name'],e.get('script_name'),e.get('aliases'),e.get('dob'),e.get('ids')) if e else '')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
